        "message": "Living together makes it trickier since you see them every day. Here are two practical ways to protect your privacy under the same roof: 1. **Use a repeatable \"broken record\" line:** Pick one neutral sentence and say the exact same thing every single time they ask, with no extra details. Something like: *\"Nothing new. If there's ever someone important, you'll be the first to know.\"* If they get the exact same non-answer every time, asking stops being interesting. 2. **Control the visual and audio cues:** Keep dating apps, messaging, and calls strictly in your private space or when you're out of the house. Fewer visible prompts usually means fewer questions. If they push after your standard line, keep it low-drama and step away into your own space with a practical exit, like going to your room to finish a task.",
